Cleaning philosophy and rules:

Always copy or back up dataset you are correcting
Work left to right through each column
    Names   =PROPER(TRIM(CLEAN(A3)))
      Text to column to split full name into first and last
      Merge, =TEXTJOIN   (=CONCAT will leave extra blank space if blank cell such as middle initial column is blank)
        
    Email Addresses, URLs, or Product IDs: PROPER will capitalize the first letter of everything. This turns john.doe@email.com into John.Doe@Email.Com. Use =LOWER(TRIM(CLEAN(A3))) for emails instead.
        
    State Abbreviations or Capitalized Acronyms: PROPER will turn "USA" or "NY" into "Usa" or "Ny". Use =UPPER(TRIM(CLEAN(A3))) for codes.
    
    Currency, Salary etc.:   often best to remove special characters (dollar sign). switch to number to prevent issues with SQL converting it to text due to $ sign.
    
